 F1-score of approximately **0.771**, while **Web Attack - XSS** achieved an F1-score of approximately **0.372**.\n","\n","The Web Attack - XSS class is particularly challenging. Only **42 of 130** test samples were correctly classified, while **85 samples were classified as Web Attack - Brute Force**.\n","\n","This indicates a strong similarity in the network-level characteristics of these two web-attack categories within the available feature space.\n","\n","Therefore, the overall accuracy of 99.57% should not be interpreted as uniformly high detection performance across every attack category. The class-level results demonstrate the importance of macro-averaged metrics and confusion-matrix analysis in cybersecurity classification tasks."],"metadata":{"id":"qmm7YK9AejIR"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Confusion Matrix Analysis\n","\n","A confusion matrix was used to examine how the XGBoost model classified each traffic category and to identify specific patterns of misclassification.\n","\n","The rows represent the actual traffic classes, while the columns represent the predicted classes. Correct predictions appear along the main diagonal, while off-diagonal values represent misclassified observations."],"metadata":{"id":"fj3aJDZDeoHm"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# XGBoost Confusion Matrix\n","\n","from sklearn.metrics import confusion_matrix\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","cm = confusion_matrix(\n","    y_test_encoded,\n","    y_pred_xgb_encoded\n",")\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(13, 10))\n","\n","plt.imshow(cm, interpolation=\"nearest\")\n","plt.title(\"XGBoost Confusion Matrix\")\n","plt.colorbar()\n","\n","tick_marks = range(len(label_encoder.classes_))\n","\n","plt.xticks(\n","    tick_marks,\n","    label_encoder.classes_,\n","    rotation=90\n",")\n","\n","plt.yticks(\n","    tick_marks,\n","    label_encoder.classes_\n",")\n","\n","plt.xlabel(\"Predicted Label\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"True Label\")\n","\n","# Add values inside cells\n","